1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,055
This is the A-One Steels India I P O, a mainboard offer,

2
00:00:04,055 --> 00:00:08,544
open from the twenty-fourth to the twenty-eighth of September,

3
00:00:08,544 --> 00:00:09,557
closing today.

4
00:00:10,057 --> 00:00:13,011
The price band is ₹385 to ₹405.

5
00:00:13,011 --> 00:00:18,824
Every figure here comes from the final red herring prospectus

6
00:00:18,824 --> 00:00:20,825
and exchange notices;

7
00:00:20,825 --> 00:00:24,541
the final price is fixed after bidding,

8
00:00:24,541 --> 00:00:28,639
so valuations are computed at the ₹405 cap.

9
00:00:29,139 --> 00:00:30,376
First, the business.

10
00:00:30,876 --> 00:00:35,570
A-One Steels is a backward-integrated steel maker based in Karnataka,

11
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:39,175
selling a range of steel products across south India.

12
00:00:39,675 --> 00:00:45,157
The RHP highlights green-energy use and a certified green product portfolio.

13
00:00:45,657 --> 00:00:49,077
FY26 was a recovery year:

14
00:00:49,077 --> 00:00:54,959
the EBITDA margin rose to 7.29% from 4.91%.

15
00:00:55,459 --> 00:00:57,059
The financial checkpoint.

16
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:10,715
FY26 revenue was ₹4,167.33 Cr, against ₹3,544.37 Cr in FY25,

17
00:01:10,715 --> 00:01:14,881
a change of 17.58%.

18
00:01:15,381 --> 00:01:23,424
Profit after tax was ₹127.41 Cr, a margin of 3.06%.

19
00:01:23,924 --> 00:01:25,183
Context matters.

20
00:01:25,683 --> 00:01:29,638
FY25 profit was only ₹7.71 Cr,

21
00:01:29,638 --> 00:01:38,077
so the jump to ₹127.41 Cr shows how cyclical steel earnings are.

22
00:01:38,577 --> 00:01:44,301
Net debt was ₹985.37 Cr at March 2026,

23
00:01:44,301 --> 00:01:48,519
with debt to equity of 1.17.

24
00:01:49,019 --> 00:01:53,008
The offer size at the cap is ₹405.00 Cr.

25
00:01:53,508 --> 00:01:58,123
₹355.00 Cr is fresh issue that goes into the company,

26
00:01:58,123 --> 00:02:04,132
and ₹50.00 Cr is an offer for sale that goes to selling shareholders.

27
00:02:04,632 --> 00:02:08,825
So 87.65% of the deal is new capital,

28
00:02:08,825 --> 00:02:13,699
and 12.35% is an exit for existing holders.

29
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:15,521
Where does the money go?

30
00:02:16,021 --> 00:02:21,462
Of the ₹355.00 Cr fresh issue, ₹250.00 Cr prepays debt,

31
00:02:21,462 --> 00:02:26,112
and the rest is for general corporate purposes.

32
00:02:26,612 --> 00:02:31,625
The ₹50.00 Cr offer for sale goes to promoter selling shareholders.

33
00:02:32,125 --> 00:02:38,995
Eligible employees get a ₹38 discount in a small ₹2 Cr reserved portion.

34
00:02:39,495 --> 00:02:40,497
Valuation.

35
00:02:40,997 --> 00:02:43,577
At the ₹405 cap,

36
00:02:43,577 --> 00:02:51,963
the price is 21.93x FY26 earnings of ₹18.47 a share.

37
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:56,761
The RHP's peers trade higher:

38
00:02:56,761 --> 00:03:00,466
Shyam Metalics at 28.31x,

39
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:06,543
Jai Balaji 45.76x and M S P Steel 61.52x.

40
00:03:07,043 --> 00:03:11,014
But a single strong year after a weak one makes any P E on

41
00:03:11,014 --> 00:03:12,589
steel earnings fragile.

42
00:03:13,089 --> 00:03:14,583
Now balance the evidence.

43
00:03:15,083 --> 00:03:16,894
Watch-out:

44
00:03:16,894 --> 00:03:21,785
FY25 PAT was only ₹7.71 Cr:

45
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:25,770
earnings are cyclical.

46
00:03:25,770 --> 00:03:27,400
Strength:

47
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:35,371
FY26 PAT ₹127.41 Cr on ₹4,167.33 Cr revenue.

48
00:03:35,871 --> 00:03:37,369
Watch-out:

49
00:03:37,369 --> 00:03:41,863
Net debt ₹985.37 Cr, D/E 1.17.

50
00:03:41,863 --> 00:03:43,212
Strength:

51
00:03:43,212 --> 00:03:49,055
₹250.00 Cr of fresh money prepays debt.

52
00:03:49,555 --> 00:03:50,974
Watch-out:

53
00:03:50,974 --> 00:03:54,097
Thin 3.06% PAT margin.

54
00:03:54,097 --> 00:03:55,375
Strength:

55
00:03:55,375 --> 00:04:00,627
21.93x P/E, below listed steel peers.

56
00:04:01,127 --> 00:04:02,257
How to apply.

57
00:04:02,757 --> 00:04:07,388
The minimum bid is one lot of 37 shares,

58
00:04:07,388 --> 00:04:10,629
which is ₹14,985 at the cap.

59
00:04:11,129 --> 00:04:14,605
Retail investors can bid up to two lakh rupees,

60
00:04:14,605 --> 00:04:18,745
and allotment is by lottery if retail is oversubscribed.

61
00:04:19,245 --> 00:04:23,788
Check live subscription on the N S E or B S E website,

62
00:04:23,788 --> 00:04:25,219
not social media.

63
00:04:25,719 --> 00:04:26,679
Let's recap.

64
00:04:27,179 --> 00:04:33,421
FY26 revenue ₹4,167.33 Cr, profit ₹127.41 Cr.

65
00:04:33,421 --> 00:04:42,022
The offer is ₹405.00 Cr, of which ₹50.00 Cr is offer for sale.

66
00:04:42,022 --> 00:04:47,571
Valuation is 21.93x earnings at the cap.

67
00:04:47,571 --> 00:04:52,288
The minimum investment is ₹14,985.

68
00:04:52,788 --> 00:04:56,962
This video is public-source education from the red herring

69
00:04:56,962 --> 00:04:59,264
prospectus and exchange notices.

70
00:04:59,264 --> 00:05:03,222
It is not investment advice and not a buy or sell call.

71
00:05:03,222 --> 00:05:05,021
Read the final documents,

72
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:07,900
check live subscription on the exchange,

73
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:10,634
and consult a SEBI-registered adviser.

74
00:05:10,634 --> 00:05:12,073
Thanks for watching.

